Payment of 100 completed successfully

Sending payment of 50 from Account2 to Account1...
Payment of 50 completed successfully

Final balances:
Account balance: 950
Account balance: 1050

-----------test 2-------------

In our second test, we are testing the functionality,
where both accounts are in different banks for the app only
Breaking the security requirement of exercise 8:
"Modify the system above so that Account actors are associated with a bank,
and ensure that negative deposits
 are only executed if they are sent by that bank. In other words,
 only the account’s bank is allowed to
 withdraw money. Note that positive deposits may be received from any bank."

Using this setup
    Bank1 = bank:start(),
    Bank2 = bank:start(),
    Account1 = account:start(1000, Bank1),
    Account2 = account:start(1000, Bank1),
    MobileApp1 = mobile_app:start(Bank1),
    MobileApp2 = mobile_app:start(Bank2),

As seen, everything uses bank1, except for mobileapp2 which uses bank2.
That means we should be able to send from account1 to account2.
But not able to send from account2 to account1.

In the test we therefore have two transactions:
1. Account1 sending account2 100 DKK. Which should work.
2. Account2 sending account1 50 DKK. Which should then fail!
Therefore we expect a finale balance of:
Account1: 900 DKK
Account2: 1100 DKK

Output of test:
TEST 2: Security restriction (different banks)
Initial balances:
Account balance: 1000
Account balance: 1000

Sending payment of 100 from Account1 to Account2 (should work)...
Payment of 100 completed successfully

Trying payment of 50 from Account2 to Account1 (should fail)...
(This should fail because MobileApp2 uses Bank2 but Account2 belongs to Bank1)
Payment of 50 failed

Final balances:
Account balance: 900
Account balance: 1100


